<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta content='text/html; charset=UTF-8' http-equiv='Content-Type' />
  </head>
  <body>
    <h2>Your Public Calendar Link is Expiring Soon</h2>

    <p>Hello <%= @user.name || @user.email %>,</p>

    <p>
      This is a reminder that your public link for <strong><%= @calendar.name %></strong>
      will expire in <strong><%= @days_remaining %> days</strong> on
      <strong><%= @expires_at.strftime("%B %d, %Y at %I:%M %p %Z") %></strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      After this date, anyone using this link will no longer be able to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>View your availability</li>
      <li>Book appointments</li>
      <li>Access calendar information</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What should you do?</h3>

    <p>
      If you want to continue sharing this calendar publicly, you have two options:
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Extend the current link</strong> - Keep the same URL and extend its expiry date
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Generate a new link</strong> - Create a fresh link with a new expiry date
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      You can manage your public calendar links from your Callab dashboard.
    </p>

    <hr/>

    <p style="color: #666; font-size: 12px;">
      This is an automated message from Callab. Public links expire for security reasons
      to ensure your calendar information stays protected.
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
